course: dictionary
lesson: 5097
title: Interfere: one word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To interfere means to get involved in something when nobody asked you to. In «Nobody interferes with him», the word «nobody» is the clue: people leave Badger alone, so interfere here means to bother or meddle.
explain: To interfere with something means to stop it from working or happening properly. «Do not interfere with the alarm» tells us the alarm must keep working. Try your meaning in the sentence: "Do not stop the alarm from working properly" makes sense.
explain: The same word can mean something different in science. «Most crews also follow a rule: do not interfere.» In a safety rule, it means do not get in the way of the work. When you meet interfere, read the words around it to find which meaning fits.
fact: Interfere means to get involved in something when you are not wanted.
fact: Interfere with something means to stop it from working or happening properly.
fact: In science, when waves interfere, they meet and add or cancel each other.
fact: «Interfere» is a verb, so it changes: interferes, interfered, interfering.
fact: Two useful phrases are «interfere with» and «interfere in».
exercise: «Badger lives right in the heart of it» and «Nobody interferes with him.» What does interferes mean here? | Looks after him kindly | Helps him find food | *Bothers or meddles with him | Feeds him every day
exercise: «Do not interfere with the alarm.» What does interfere with mean? | Sing along with it | Admire its design | *Stop it from working properly | Make it louder
exercise: When waves interfere, what happens? | They turn into rain | They hide behind rocks | They only ever get smaller | *They meet and add or cancel each other
test: Which word means to get involved when you are not wanted? | Interest | *Interfere | Attend | Assist
test: Which is the correct past tense of interfere? | Interfer | Interfering | *Interfered | Interferring
exam: Why is the rule «do not interfere» important for a safety crew? | *Because interfering can stop safety work from working properly | Because it helps the waves meet | Because meddling makes the job more fun | Because it makes the job longer
